# Third-party Ignition modules this stack uses, and where each one comes from.
#
# Read by scripts/get-modules.sh. Five pipe-separated fields:
#
#   filename | gateways | sha256 | source | what it is
#
#   gateways  comma-separated stack names -- the file is placed in modules/<stack>/
#             for each one, because ign-modules.sh installs per gateway.
#   sha256    always present. It is the point: a module is a signed binary that
#             the gateway will execute, and "it downloaded without an error" is
#             not the same as "it is the file we tested against".
#   source    an https URL, or MANUAL for a module with no unauthenticated
#             download. A MANUAL module can still be fetched automatically by
#             pointing MODULES_MIRROR at somewhere your team controls -- see
#             docs/PORTABLE.md. The hash is checked either way.
#
# VERSIONS ARE PINNED TO THE IGNITION VERSION IN stacks/*/compose.yaml (8.3.9).
# A module built for 8.1 will not load on 8.3 and vice versa; the gateway logs
# a version-mismatch and carries on without it, which looks like the module
# simply not working. When you move the gateways to a new Ignition version,
# update this file in the same commit.
#
# Where each URL came from:
#   * Embr Charts is MIT-licensed and published as a GitHub release asset, so
#     it can be fetched directly and verified. Confirmed byte-identical to the
#     copy this stack was built against, 04/08/2026.
#   * The Cirrus Link MQTT modules ARE fetchable, which we had wrong until
#     07/08/2026. The downloads page puts a HubSpot form in front of them, but
#     it also carries a "Skip form and download directly" link, and that link's
#     href is the URL below. The catch is that the file lives on
#     releases.inductiveautomation.com, which answers 403 AccessDenied to a
#     request with no `Referer` -- so curl failed while a browser succeeded, and
#     the whole host read as authenticated when it is only hotlink-protected.
#     get-modules.sh sends the referer; see referer_for() there.
#     Corollary, learned the hard way 21/09/2026: a 403 from that host means
#     "no referer", NOT "that version exists but is restricted". Probing made-up
#     version numbers therefore 403s for every one of them and proves nothing.
#     The version list is Cirrus Link's own 8.3 release notes
#     (docs.chariot.io/display/CLD83/Ignition+8.3+Compatible+Release+Notes):
#     5.0.4, 28/07/2026, is the newest for Ignition 8.3 -- there is no 5.0.5,
#     5.1.x or 5.2.0. We are current; all three modules move together.
#     The list of every module and version lives at
#     https://inductiveautomation.com/downloads/third-party-modules/<ignition-version>
#     and the URLs follow .../third-party/cirrus-link/<module-version>/<file>.
#   * The Architecture Builder is NOT the Ignition Exchange resource we long
#     recorded it as. Exchange 2693 ("ArchitectureBuildOut") is a project export
#     for Ignition 8.1, by a different author, and needs an account. The module
#     is published openly on GitHub by its actual author, MIT-licensed, and
#     needs no account and no referer. This repo already named that repository
#     in scripts/upstream.pins and docs/ARCH-BUILDER.md -- only the manifest was
#     still pointing at the Exchange, which is why nobody noticed.
#
# THE ASSET NAME CARRIES NO VERSION. Upstream publishes every release as plain
# `ArchitectureBuilder.modl`; the version exists only in the tag. The filename
# in the first column is what the file is SAVED as, so the version is restored
# on the way in -- do not "fix" the URL to match the filename, it 404s.

Embr-Charts-Ignition83-6.0.1.modl | ignition | 40d0989233f19433552c60d473d7f2fd8bf0af4f173c56427388b826a40954de | https://github.com/mussonindustrial/embr/releases/download/releases/8.3/2026.6.17/Embr-Charts-Ignition83-6.0.1.modl | Perspective chart components (unused by the dashboard now, kept for the Exchange demo)

MQTT-Engine-signed.modl | ignition | 9e78753237e381de8ad62bc6640680fd05e5525ea5b702e0d73098a55773bede | https://releases.inductiveautomation.com/third-party/cirrus-link/5.0.4/MQTT-Engine-signed.modl | Cirrus Link MQTT Engine 5.0.4 -- the hub subscribes to Sparkplug with this

MQTT-Distributor-signed.modl | ignition,ignition-broker | 3980500716ed7d9093ca12f3e48d545a098277b755be43229da7891b99835370 | https://releases.inductiveautomation.com/third-party/cirrus-link/5.0.4/MQTT-Distributor-signed.modl | Cirrus Link MQTT Distributor 5.0.4 -- the broker-in-Ignition investigation (docs/MQTT-DISTRIBUTOR.md): inside the hub (the backup gets it by module sync) and alone on the standalone broker gateway. Must match Engine's version

MQTT-Transmission-signed.modl | ignition-edge1,ignition-edge2,ignition-edge3,ignition-edge4 | 0b5b472a39f428b86442ea85faafa5697dac50aef9931d9ef71edda8e4f81ebb | https://releases.inductiveautomation.com/third-party/cirrus-link/5.0.4/MQTT-Transmission-signed.modl | Cirrus Link MQTT Transmission 5.0.4 -- each edge publishes Sparkplug with this

